# MeTTa compatibility xfail list
# Format:  <relative-path>  <STATUS>:<CATEGORY>:<id>  [free-form notes]
# STATUS  ∈ COMPILE_FAIL | RUN_EXCEPTION | ASSERT_FAIL
# CATEGORY ∈ FEATURE_PENDING | STDLIB_GAP | SEMANTIC_DIVERGENCE | KNOWN_BUG
#
# A test is EXPECTED_FAIL when its actual STATUS matches the line.
# A mismatch (test fails for a different reason) is reported as REGRESSION.
# A test now passing is reported as UNEXPECTED_PASS — remove its line.
#
# The runner skips files imported by other files in the suite (modules).
# So entries here only need to cover files that run as standalone tests.

# f1_imports COMPILES and runs. The multivalued-tuple-lift blocker is FIXED: the first assert's
# `((let $x (get-atoms &self) (get-type $x)))` now lifts into
#   flat-map?(\$v. map?(\$e. ($e), ((\ ($x) (get-type $x)) $v)), (get-atoms &self))
# instead of freezing as an Atom[] holding a lambda. The `contains`/`is-space` and the first
# `import!` asserts pass too.
#
# :56 — the `(match &m (= (f 2) $x) $x)` = `(g 3)` assertion — now PASSES. It needed four things,
# all landed: the match result evaluated (`matchReduceDeep`), RUN-TIME visibility (a module's
# load-time `&self` rebound to the module's own space), COMPILE-TIME ordered visibility (a `!`-run
# resolves only against modules imported into `&self` before it), and applicative reduction of an
# inert application's arguments (`(g (+ 1 2))` -> `(g 3)`).
#
# The file now stops at **:65**, `!(assertEqual (f 2) 103)`. That one line had TWO independent
# pre-existing causes; the first is fixed, the second is what fails now.
#
#  1. FIXED — the module compile queue was sorted by PATH, so f1_moduleA was resolved before
#     f1_moduleC and its `(g (+ 1 $x))` resolved to nothing and was emitted as inert data. The
#     queue is now ordered by the import graph. Repro of the general bug (both directions):
#     a module `amid` importing `zdep` failed while the same pair named `cmid`/`bdep` worked.
#
#  2. `Number` is not a type. `FunctionRewriter.asType()` has no entry for it, so
#     `(: g (-> Number Number))` erases to `(-> Atom Int)` — and an `Atom` PARAMETER carries
#     hyperon's meta-type semantics "do not reduce the argument" (FunctionGenerator ~:1428). So
#     `g` is handed the unreduced `(+ 1 2)` and its body's `Grounded` unwrap throws
#     ClassCastException. Nothing to do with imports; one file reproduces it:
#       (: r (-> Number Number))  (= (r $x) (+ $x 100))  !(assertEqual (r (+ 1 2)) 103)
#     The same file with `(: r (-> Int Int))` passes. The fix is a real `Number` type that erases
#     to a reference like `Atom` but is NOT the meta-Atom, so the argument is evaluated and
#     arrives as a `Grounded` number.
f1_imports.metta            RUN_EXCEPTION:FEATURE_PENDING:number-type-erases-to-meta-atom    :65 `(f 2)` -> CCE inside f1_moduleC.g, handed the unreduced `(+ 1 2)`. See notes above
